@*
    The design system's row-actions kebab, with the menu left to the caller.

    `.data-table__actions` in the handoff's list archetype holds exactly one
    control - a `btn btn--icon btn--sm` opening a `.ra__menu` (see
    PageList.dc.html, whose menu is "Use template / Duplicate / Edit metadata /
    Archive"). Several admin lists were still rendering the pre-redesign row of
    full text buttons instead, and that is what #574 turned out to be: the
    actions column was 200-314px of a ~940px table, so the table's min-content
    opened the whole content column and the right-hand end of the page was
    CLIPPED - `.app__content` is overflow-x: hidden, so it was not even
    scrollable. At 1100px that cost /admin/cookbook five unreachable Delete
    buttons; at 880px, the page's own New recipe button.

    RowActionsMenu.razor is the Object Explorer's fixed three-item version of
    this; this one is the shell for lists whose entries differ per page.

    Open/close, one-at-a-time, close on outside click / scroll / Escape are
    owned globally by wwwroot/row-actions-menu.js, which is delegated and
    matches on the `data-ra-toggle` attribute - so this works on a static-SSR
    page with no Blazor circuit, which /site-admin/users is.
*@

<span class="ra">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--icon@(Small ? " btn--sm" : "")" data-ra-toggle
            title="@Label" aria-label="@Label"
            aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <Icon Name="@Icon" Width="15" Height="15" />
    </button>

    <div class="ra__menu menu" role="menu">@ChildContent</div>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The menu entries: `.menu__item` links, buttons or forms.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Accessible name for the trigger. Defaults to the generic wording; give a
    /// row-specific one ("Actions for CRONUS Standard") where a screen-reader
    /// user would otherwise meet a column of identical buttons.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "More actions";

    /// <summary>
    /// The trigger's glyph. A row's menu is the vertical kebab; a command bar's overflow
    /// ("More options" in PageUpgrades.dc.html) is the horizontal one.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string Icon { get; set; } = "ellipsis-vertical";

    /// <summary>The row-sized trigger. Off for a command bar, whose buttons are full height.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Small { get; set; } = true;
}
